WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.400
Welcome to DBL Group's TalentHub!

2
00:00:03.919 --> 00:00:08.000
A candidate never signs in to TalentHub:

3
00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.560
everything happens on public pages
and through links in emails.

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.480
In this video we'll see
how a candidate applies,

5
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:21.280
how they take the tests and interviews,
and how they join. Let's get started!

6
00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:25.910
The path: apply, the status tracker,
a test, interviews,

7
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:30.870
the onboarding portal, the offer, the
Code of Conduct, the appointment letter.

8
00:00:31.870 --> 00:00:36.350
Knowing it as HR makes a candidate's
questions easy to answer.

9
00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:41.540
The careers page lists every open post,
with a search,

10
00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:46.020
and a unit filter when there is more than
one unit. A listing shows the post, unit,

11
00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.260
department, place, how many, a summary,
and Apply by, the last day to apply.

12
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:53.500
After that day the post leaves the page.

13
00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:59.090
Apply Now. The form is short: name, email,

14
00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:04.839
mobile, expected salary, a figure
or Negotiable, and the CV as a PDF.

15
00:01:04.959 --> 00:01:06.329
Submit application.

16
00:01:06.679 --> 00:01:09.629
Submit opens Verify your email.
A six-digit code is emailed,

17
00:01:09.879 --> 00:01:15.199
valid ten minutes. Enter it
and the application is in,

18
00:01:15.319 --> 00:01:19.959
with an Application ID starting APP.
A confirmation goes by email too.

19
00:01:20.309 --> 00:01:26.029
Track application opens the tracker; so
does View Application Status in the email.

20
00:01:26.149 --> 00:01:31.237
Enter the email and every application
shows its ID and stage: Applied,

21
00:01:31.357 --> 00:01:36.109
Shortlisted, Interview, Final Round,
Selected, or Not Selected.

22
00:01:36.629 --> 00:01:38.869
The candidate can check any time.

23
00:01:39.219 --> 00:01:44.259
The confirmation email carries the
Application ID, the post and the tracker's

24
00:01:44.379 --> 00:01:49.939
link. That ID is enough when talking to
HR; the pipeline's search finds it too.

25
00:01:50.289 --> 00:01:55.449
There are other ways in: from BDJobs,
by employee referral, or a CV handed over.

26
00:01:55.569 --> 00:02:01.409
With a referral, both the candidate
and the referrer get a letter.

27
00:02:01.759 --> 00:02:04.369
Two posts with the same email?

28
00:02:04.489 --> 00:02:08.259
The tracker lists both,
separate IDs, separate stages.

29
00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:14.159
Not Selected shows here too; the regret
letter is separate, if HR sends it.

30
00:02:14.509 --> 00:02:18.159
If the recruiter assigns the AI
Proficiency Test, the link comes by email.

31
00:02:18.749 --> 00:02:21.749
Opening it does not start the clock;
Start Test does.

32
00:02:21.869 --> 00:02:28.229
Full screen; leaving the tab
shows a warning, and HR is told.

33
00:02:29.109 --> 00:02:30.589
At most three attempts.

34
00:02:30.939 --> 00:02:36.659
The interview invitation email: the round,
Dhaka time, a Meet link or the venue.

35
00:02:37.099 --> 00:02:41.099
If it moves, another email
with the new and the old time.

36
00:02:41.449 --> 00:02:46.849
On the day: in person,
at the venue and room in the email,

37
00:02:46.969 --> 00:02:52.129
before the time. Online, on the Meet link,

38
00:02:52.249 --> 00:02:56.729
also from the calendar invite.
Times are Dhaka, GMT+6.

39
00:02:57.079 --> 00:03:00.799
And those who did not go through
may get DBL's regret letter,

40
00:03:00.919 --> 00:03:03.159
only if HR sends it, and only once.

41
00:03:03.509 --> 00:03:05.939
Once selected,
the link to the onboarding portal.

42
00:03:06.059 --> 00:03:10.549
Welcome to DBL Group.
All the joining paperwork lives here.

43
00:03:10.899 --> 00:03:14.668
Your documents,
section by section: photographs,

44
00:03:14.788 --> 00:03:18.699
academic, professional,
experience, identity, financial.

45
00:03:19.539 --> 00:03:25.059
Each slot takes PDF, JPG or PNG. Statuses:

46
00:03:25.179 --> 00:03:30.259
Pending review, Verified, or Rejected;
a rejected one is uploaded again.

47
00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:32.538
Some slots repeat:

48
00:03:32.658 --> 00:03:38.409
more than one professional certificate,
each added with its name.

49
00:03:38.529 --> 00:03:41.449
Photographs are hard copy,
only ticked on the portal.

50
00:03:42.209 --> 00:03:45.649
Every slot carries a short
hint of what is wanted.

51
00:03:45.999 --> 00:03:50.519
Four NID particulars are typed
and saved: name, address,

52
00:03:50.639 --> 00:03:55.639
date of birth, number, because they
print on the appointment letter.

53
00:03:56.159 --> 00:03:59.039
And a signature image,
cropped three to one.

54
00:03:59.389 --> 00:04:05.268
If HR rejects a document, the slot turns
Rejected, say for an unreadable scan.

55
00:04:05.388 --> 00:04:07.789
Upload a new file
and it is Pending review again.

56
00:04:08.139 --> 00:04:14.088
When the offer arrives,
it waits on the portal.

57
00:04:14.208 --> 00:04:17.699
First, your tentative date of joining.

58
00:04:18.022 --> 00:04:20.872
Accept offer signs it with the
signature you already gave;

59
00:04:20.992 --> 00:04:25.349
if there is none, you add it right there.
To turn it down,

60
00:04:25.469 --> 00:04:28.369
I need to decline this offer,
with a reason, which HR sees.

61
00:04:28.489 --> 00:04:32.689
Finally the Code of Conduct:
read, tick, sign. Then the

62
00:04:33.449 --> 00:04:39.129
signed offer stays on the portal as a PDF,
and the appointment letter comes by email.

63
00:04:39.479 --> 00:04:44.063
Everything one candidate receives:
the application confirmation,

64
00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:48.342
the test link, interview invitations,
a regret letter,

65
00:04:48.462 --> 00:04:53.599
the portal link, the offer, the Code
of Conduct, the appointment letter.

66
00:04:54.439 --> 00:04:58.320
Each ends with the note:
automated, do not reply.

67
00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:04.737
In between comes the medical
appointment email too: when, where,

68
00:05:04.857 --> 00:05:08.590
the reference number. After the
onboarding documents, before the offer.

69
00:05:08.940 --> 00:05:12.900
Security.
No application without a verified email.

70
00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:16.660
Every link is one person's and expires.

71
00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:21.180
CVs and documents sit in Google Drive
and open only through signed links.

72
00:05:21.530 --> 00:05:23.970
An expired link says so on the page.

73
00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:28.914
HR sends a new one: for the portal,
the recruiter's Send portal link;

74
00:05:29.034 --> 00:05:30.810
for the test, a new attempt.

75
00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.560
What candidates ask. No code?

76
00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:39.480
Resend after sixty seconds,
check the spam folder.

77
00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:44.960
Applied for two posts?
The tracker lists both. Document rejected?

78
00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:50.760
Upload a clearer copy in the same slot,
and ask HR if you are unsure why.

79
00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:53.390
Declined by mistake? Tell HR;

80
00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:58.349
a revised offer can be accepted again.
And the signature is given once;

81
00:05:58.469 --> 00:06:03.910
it is used for both the offer
and the Code of Conduct.

82
00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:10.780
In short. The careers page, Apply Now,
the code, the Application ID, the tracker.

83
00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:18.380
Test and interview links by email.
On the portal: documents, NID, signature,

84
00:06:19.430 --> 00:06:23.530
the offer, the Code of Conduct. The full
guide is a PDF under Tutorials. Thank you.

